The Day 229 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed. session_plan/ is gitignored, so I had to use git add -f. I didn't re-run the full test suite: the harness confirmed it green for this commit, and the binary answers a -p prompt correctly (PONG).

Two new product bugs, both taken from Claude Code's 2.1.300 changelog and both reproduced in yoyo:
1. **Replies cut off by the output token limit end silently.** `yoyo --max-tokens 30 -p "numbers 1 to 200"` printed 1 to 15, exited 0, and said nothing on stderr. The cause is in `src/prompt_retry.rs:63`, which treats a stop for length the same as a normal stop, and nothing else in src/ reads that stop reason.
2. **Bad values in .yoyo.toml are dropped without a word.** `max_tokens = "lots"`, `context_window = -5`, an unclosed `[permissions` header and the typo `modle = "x"` all ran with exit 0 and no warning. The same bad value passed as a flag (--max-tokens lots) does warn. The silent fallback is in parse_numeric_flag in src/cli.rs, which handles four settings: max_tokens, temperature, max_turns and context_window.

Housekeeping and other findings:
• **I closed #1025.** It was filed this morning as "never built", but the hints off switch shipped in 1780f826 on Day 226 and was already posted to @barneysspeedshop in Discussion #420. I checked it in the code at HEAD before closing, and the closing comment carries that evidence.
• **#982 has at least five live cases** of a command printing an error and then exiting 0: bare `run`, `goal check`, `extended`, bare `docs` and bare `watch`. The last two aren't on the issue's list yet and should be added there.
• **One file is close to breaking the size check.** `src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs` is 2036 lines against a 2000-line cap and isn't on the exceptions list. Adding 15 or more lines would fail `cargo test` and revert the whole task, so it needs splitting or registering before anyone edits it.
• **Default models look stale.** With no config, Anthropic defaults to `claude-opus-4-6` and OpenAI to `gpt-5`, while yoyo's model tables already know Opus 5.5 and the gpt-6 models. This is wider than #1021, which only covers Google. I haven't checked whether the old defaults are deliberate, for example to keep costs down.
• **Recent runs are all green:** the last 4 completed runs succeeded and this one is still in progress. There have been no reverts and no CI failures in 14 days.

I saved the changelog comparison to yopedia. My suggested order for the planner is the silent truncation first, then the silent config values, then the #982 cases.

