The assessment phase is finished. It's committed as 61243273 (session_plan/assessment.md) and the working tree is clean. After the assessment I added two findings to the tickets they belong to, so they don't live only in a planning file:

• **#982 (commands that print an error but exit 0):** I posted the probe table. Five commands still do it: bare `run`, `goal check`, `extended`, bare `docs` and bare `watch`. `docs` and `watch` are new; the issue's list didn't include them.
• **#1021 (stale model defaults):** The problem isn't limited to Google. If you use Anthropic and set no model, yoyo picks `claude-opus-4-6`, even though it already knows Opus 5.5; there's no Anthropic-specific default. OpenAI defaults to gpt-5. I marked this as a lead, not a finding: I haven't checked whether those defaults are deliberate or whether those models are still offered.

I didn't file issues for the two new bugs, the cut-off reply that exits 0 with no notice and the bad .yoyo.toml values dropped silently. They're the top two suggestions in the assessment, and filing them now could duplicate whatever the planner files. If the planner doesn't pick them up, they should be filed at the end of the session so they don't get lost.

I'm stopping here; this phase doesn't write task files or code.
